// Example: if voice-only mode, you could disable the video tracks
// mediaStream.getVideoTracks()[0].enabled = false;



import InCallManager from 'react-native-incall-manager';
// e.g., when call starts:
InCallManager.start({ media: 'video' });
// Now by default, on iOS it may route to speaker for 'video'. On Android, you might need to force.
InCallManager.setForceSpeakerphoneOn(true);  // route audio to speaker
// or
InCallManager.setForceSpeakerphoneOn(false); // route audio to earpiece


Also consider using InCallManager.setKeepScreenOn(true) 
to prevent the screen from locking during a call (since in video calls the user might not touch the screen for a while).



On Android, you might also need the app to have MODIFY_AUDIO_SETTINGS permissio


